## ============================================================================
## Logging / Telemetry
## ============================================================================
#
# HYPERDX_LOG_LEVEL=info
# USAGE_STATS_ENABLED=false

## ============================================================================
## ClickHouse Sources
## ============================================================================
## Compose seeds these from config/hyperdx/default-sources.json, which the
## service mounts and passes as DEFAULT_SOURCES_FILE. Set the JSON inline here to
## override that file for this deployment.
#
# DEFAULT_SOURCES=

## ============================================================================
## Auth
## ============================================================================
## Compose runs `header-dev`: dfe-hyperdx-proxy stamps every request with one
## fixed operator identity, so there is no login and whoever reaches the port IS
## that operator. Change WHO with DFE_HYPERDX_IDENTITY_EMAIL /
## DFE_HYPERDX_IDENTITY_GROUPS in .env, and gate the port with the `auth`
## profile, a VPN or a tunnel.
##
## `oidc-proxy` is the Kubernetes posture -- it verifies the engine's JWT and
## needs DFE_ENGINE_JWKS_URL, which no Compose deployment has. Setting it here
## turns every request into a 401.
#
# DFE_AUTH_MODE=header-dev
# HYPERDX_API_KEY=